## Task add notification
## $employeeTask.task.name(EdsTask) - new task
## $employeeTask(EdsUser) - employeeTask of this alert
## $user(EdsUser) - User submitted alert
## $assignees - Comma separated list of assignees
## $date - Date this alert was submitted
## $complatedTask- Status Completed Task
## $link --

<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">

<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" />
</head><body><p>Dear $employeeTask.projectEmployee.employeeDepartment.employee.getName(),</p>
<p>Please be informed that predecessor task - $complatedTask to your $employeeTask.task.name has been marked as completed on $date.</p>
<p>Task Name: $employeeTask.task.name<br />
Task Number: $employeeTask.task.number<br />
Project: $employeeTask.task.project.name<br />  Assignee(s): $assignees</p>
<p>Click <a href="$host/ProjectManagement.html?link=$link" title="View task" target="_blank">here</a>
to view the task</p><p>* If you are not able to click on the link, you can instead copy and paste the following address in to your web browser: </p>
<p><span style="color: #0033FF">$host/ProjectManagement.html?link=$link</span></p>
</body></html>










